      {
        "title": "0. Baseline: no test infrastructure exists",
        "content": "\nThere are **zero test files** in the repo and no test runner in `package.json` (no `vitest`/`jest`, no `test` script). Every gap below is therefore total, not partial. Before any test skeleton can run, add a runner. Given this is Next.js 16 + React 19 + TS + Zod + Drizzle, **Vitest** is the fit (fast, native ESM/TS, works with `next/server` mocks via `vi.mock`). Recommended additions:\n\n```json\n// package.json\n\"devDependencies\": {\n  \"vitest\": \"^3\",\n  \"@vitejs/plugin-react\": \"^5\",\n  \"vite-tsconfig-paths\": \"^5\"\n},\n\"scripts\": {\n  \"test\": \"vitest run\",\n  \"test:watch\": \"vitest\"\n}\n```\n\nAll skeletons below assume `import { describe, it, expect, vi } from \"vitest\"`.\n\n---\n\n",
        "level": 2
      },
      {
        "title": "1. `lib/diff-chars.ts` — `diffSegments`",
        "content": "\nPure, zero I/O, highest ROI. Currently **0% covered**.\n\n**Gaps:** equal values, one-empty vs other, fully-disjoint strings, single shared char, unicode/multi-byte characters, prefix/suffix overlap edge case (e.g. `\"aaa\"` vs `\"aa\"` — repeated chars can make the suffix-scan overcount if `max` isn't respected).\n\n```ts\n// lib/diff-chars.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { diffSegments } from \"@/lib/diff-chars\";\n\ndescribe(\"diffSegments\", () => {\n  it(\"returns everything as prefix when values are identical\", () => {\n    expect(diffSegments(\"APAC\", \"APAC\")).toEqual({ prefix: \"APAC\", middle: \"\", suffix: \"\" });\n  });\n\n  it(\"finds a differing middle with shared head and tail\", () => {\n    expect(diffSegments(\"APAC\", \"APAC-SOUTH\")).toEqual({\n      prefix: \"APAC\", middle: \"\", suffix: \"\" // TODO: verify actual expected split (differs by length)\n    });\n  });\n\n  it(\"handles totally disjoint strings\", () => {\n    const r = diffSegments(\"ACC-4417\", \"ACC-2201\");\n    expect(r.prefix).toBe(\"ACC-2\");\n    // TODO: assert middle/suffix precisely\n  });\n\n  it(\"handles one side empty\", () => {\n    expect(diffSegments(\"\", \"ACME\")).toEqual({ prefix: \"\", middle: \"\", suffix: \"\" });\n  });\n\n  it(\"does not double-count overlapping prefix/suffix on repeated characters\", () => {\n    // \"aaa\" vs \"aa\" — prefix scan alone would claim prefix=2, suffix scan must\n    // respect `max - prefix` or it re-consumes the same characters.\n    const r = diffSegments(\"aaa\", \"aa\");\n    expect(r.prefix.length + r.middle.length + r.suffix.length).toBe(3);\n  });\n\n  it(\"handles unicode / combining characters without splitting a code point\", () => {\n    const r = diffSegments(\"café\", \"cafe\\u0301\"); // é vs e + combining accent\n    expect(r.prefix + r.middle + r.suffix).toBe(\"café\");\n  });\n\n  it(\"case sensitivity: differing case is a middle, not equality\", () => {\n    const r = diffSegments(\"ACME\", \"acme\");\n    expect(r.middle.length).toBeGreaterThan(0);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n",
        "level": 2
      },
      {
        "title": "2. `lib/validate-value.ts` — `foldValue`, `checkObservedValue`, `observedValues`",
        "content": "\nSecurity/correctness critical — this is the guard against a reviewer injecting a hallucinated value into the resolved hierarchy, and it must **stay in lockstep with `engine/pipeline/normalize.py`**. No cross-language contract test exists either.\n\n**Gaps:** suffix-stripping order (`\"Trellis Labs Pvt Ltd\"` — two suffixes), suffix-is-the-whole-value edge case (`folded === suffix` guard), punctuation-only input, whitespace-only candidate, empty `observed` array, both `observed` values empty, exact match vs folded match priority, case/diacritic folding (NFKD).\n\n```ts\n// lib/validate-value.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { foldValue, checkObservedValue, observedValues, LEGAL_SUFFIXES } from \"@/lib/validate-value\";\n\ndescribe(\"foldValue\", () => {\n  it(\"lowercases, strips punctuation, collapses whitespace\", () => {\n    expect(foldValue(\"ACME-INC\")).toBe(\"acme\");\n    expect(foldValue(\"Acme Inc.\")).toBe(\"acme\");\n  });\n\n  it(\"strips multiple legal suffixes in one pass\", () => {\n    expect(foldValue(\"Trellis Labs Pvt Ltd\")).toBe(\"trellis labs\");\n  });\n\n  it(\"does not strip a suffix that IS the whole value\", () => {\n    expect(foldValue(\"Ltd\")).toBe(\"ltd\");\n  });\n\n  it(\"prefers the longest matching suffix (pvt ltd over ltd)\", () => {\n    expect(foldValue(\"X Pvt Ltd\")).not.toContain(\"pvt\");\n  });\n\n  it(\"folds diacritics via NFKD\", () => {\n    expect(foldValue(\"Café\")).toBe(\"cafe\");\n  });\n\n  it(\"returns empty string for punctuation-only input\", () => {\n    expect(foldValue(\"...---\")).toBe(\"\");\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"checkObservedValue\", () => {\n  it(\"rejects an empty/whitespace-only candidate\", () => {\n    const r = checkObservedValue(\"   \", [\"ACC-4417\"]);\n    expect(r.ok).toBe(false);\n  });\n\n  it(\"rejects when observed has no real values (orphan side)\", () => {\n    const r = checkObservedValue(\"ACC-4417\", [\"\", \"  \"]);\n    expect(r.ok).toBe(false);\n  });\n\n  it(\"accepts an exact match even when a folded match also exists\", () => {\n    const r = checkObservedValue(\"ACME Inc.\", [\"ACME Inc.\", \"acme inc\"]);\n    expect(r).toEqual({ ok: true, matches: \"ACME Inc.\" });\n  });\n\n  it(\"accepts a legal normalization of an observed value\", () => {\n    const r = checkObservedValue(\"ACME\", [\"ACME Inc.\"]);\n    expect(r).toEqual({ ok: true, matches: \"ACME Inc.\" });\n  });\n\n  it(\"rejects a value that folds to neither observed value (hallucination guard)\", () => {\n    const r = checkObservedValue(\"ACC-9999\", [\"ACC-4417\", \"ACC-2201\"]);\n    expect(r.ok).toBe(false);\n    if (!r.ok) expect(r.reason).toContain(\"ACC-4417\");\n  });\n\n  it(\"trims the candidate before comparing\", () => {\n    const r = checkObservedValue(\"  ACC-4417  \", [\"ACC-4417\"]);\n    expect(r).toEqual({ ok: true, matches: \"ACC-4417\" });\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"observedValues\", () => {\n  it(\"flattens both sides and drops blank entries\", () => {\n    expect(observedValues({ a: { values: [\"X\", \"\"] }, b: { values: [\"Y\"] } })).toEqual([\"X\", \"Y\"]);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe.skip(\"cross-language parity with engine/pipeline/normalize.py::LEGAL_SUFFIXES\", () => {\n  // Integration gap: nothing asserts the TS list and the Python list stay\n  // identical. A fixture-based contract test (shared JSON list, or a snapshot\n  // compared against the Python module's output) would catch drift.\n  it(\"LEGAL_SUFFIXES matches the engine's list byte-for-byte\", () => {\n    expect(LEGAL_SUFFIXES).toEqual([/* load from engine/pipeline/normalize.py fixture */]);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n",
        "level": 2
      },
      {
        "title": "3. `lib/format.ts` — six pure formatters",
        "content": "\n**Gaps:** `formatElapsed` at exact hour boundary (3599999ms vs 3600000ms), negative ms, `formatRelative` at each threshold boundary (59s/60s, 59m/60m, 23h/24h) and with a fixed `now`, `shortRunId` with a UUID shorter than 6 hex chars (malformed input), `formatStat` with `0` vs `null` vs `undefined`, `formatConfidence` rounding (`0.005` → `\"0.01\"` vs `\"0.00\"`, banker's rounding surprises).\n\n```ts\n// lib/format.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport {\n  shortRunId, formatElapsed, formatCount, formatStat,\n  formatClockTime, formatTimestamp, formatRelative, formatConfidence,\n} from \"@/lib/format\";\n\ndescribe(\"shortRunId\", () => {\n  it(\"strips hyphens and takes 4+2 chars joined by an interpunct\", () => {\n    expect(shortRunId(\"a41f1234-c9ab-...\")).toBe(\"a41f·1c\"); // TODO verify exact slice\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"formatElapsed\", () => {\n  it(\"renders mm:ss under an hour\", () => expect(formatElapsed(65_000)).toBe(\"01:05\"));\n  it(\"renders h:mm:ss at exactly one hour\", () => expect(formatElapsed(3_600_000)).toBe(\"1:00:00\"));\n  it(\"clamps negative durations to zero\", () => expect(formatElapsed(-500)).toBe(\"00:00\"));\n  it(\"floors sub-second remainders\", () => expect(formatElapsed(999)).toBe(\"00:00\"));\n});\n\ndescribe(\"formatStat\", () => {\n  it(\"renders an em dash for null\", () => expect(formatStat(null)).toBe(\"—\"));\n  it(\"renders an em dash for undefined\", () => expect(formatStat(undefined)).toBe(\"—\"));\n  it(\"renders 0 distinctly from not-yet-computed\", () => expect(formatStat(0)).toBe(\"0\"));\n});\n\ndescribe(\"formatRelative\", () => {\n  const now = new Date(\"2026-08-08T12:00:00Z\");\n  it(\"says 'just now' under 60s\", () => expect(formatRelative(new Date(\"2026-08-08T11:59:30Z\"), now)).toBe(\"just now\"));\n  it(\"boundary at exactly 60s\", () => expect(formatRelative(new Date(\"2026-08-08T11:59:00Z\"), now)).toBe(\"1m ago\"));\n  it(\"boundary at exactly 60m\", () => expect(formatRelative(new Date(\"2026-08-08T11:00:00Z\"), now)).toBe(\"1h ago\"));\n  it(\"boundary at exactly 24h\", () => expect(formatRelative(new Date(\"2026-08-07T12:00:00Z\"), now)).toBe(\"1d ago\"));\n  it(\"handles a future date (negative delta) without throwing\", () => {\n    expect(() => formatRelative(new Date(\"2026-08-08T13:00:00Z\"), now)).not.toThrow();\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"formatConfidence\", () => {\n  it(\"always renders two decimals\", () => expect(formatConfidence(0.9)).toBe(\"0.90\"));\n  it(\"clamps/handles out-of-range input gracefully\", () => {\n    // No clamping in source — document current (possibly surprising) behavior.\n    expect(formatConfidence(1.5)).toBe(\"1.50\");\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n",
        "level": 2
      },
      {
        "title": "4. `lib/rule-trace.ts` — `deriveRuleTrace`",
        "content": "\nState-machine-shaped logic with 4 branches driven by `resolution` presence, `appliedRuleId`, and `proposedValue.length`. **No branch is tested.**\n\n**Gaps:** unresolved conflict (`resolution: null`), rule-decided-with-value (apply ran), rule-decided-no-value (shouldn't be reachable but should be asserted against), no-rule-with-value (propose ran), no-rule-no-value (escalated, nothing proposed), `appliedRuleStrategy` fallback to `appliedRuleId` when strategy is null.\n\n```ts\n// lib/rule-trace.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { deriveRuleTrace } from \"@/lib/rule-trace\";\nimport type { QueueRow } from \"@/types/queue\";\n\nfunction row(overrides: Partial<QueueRow[\"resolution\"]>, base: Partial<QueueRow> = {}): QueueRow {\n  return {\n    field: \"parentExternalId\", entityType: \"account\",\n    resolution: overrides === null ? null : { id: \"r1\", proposedValue: \"\", rationale: \"\", appliedRuleId: null, appliedRuleStrategy: null, confidence: 0, status: \"proposed\", reviewedBy: null, overrideValue: null, reviewedAt: null, ...overrides },\n    ...base,\n  } as QueueRow;\n}\n\ndescribe(\"deriveRuleTrace\", () => {\n  it(\"shows only classify (not-yet-resolved) when resolution is null\", () => {\n    const trace = deriveRuleTrace(row(null as any));\n    expect(trace).toHaveLength(1);\n    expect(trace[0].ran).toBe(false);\n  });\n\n  it(\"marks apply as ran when a rule decided and a value was proposed\", () => {\n    const trace = deriveRuleTrace(row({ appliedRuleId: \"rule-1\", appliedRuleStrategy: \"most_recent\", proposedValue: \"ACC-2201\" }));\n    const apply = trace.find((s) => s.node === \"apply\")!;\n    expect(apply.ran).toBe(true);\n    expect(apply.detail).toBe(\"ACC-2201\");\n    const propose = trace.find((s) => s.node === \"propose\")!;\n    expect(propose.ran).toBe(false);\n  });\n\n  it(\"marks propose as ran when no rule matched but a value was proposed (agent path)\", () => {\n    const trace = deriveRuleTrace(row({ appliedRuleId: null, proposedValue: \"ACC-2201\", confidence: 0.91 }));\n    const propose = trace.find((s) => s.node === \"propose\")!;\n    expect(propose.ran).toBe(true);\n    expect(propose.detail).toContain(\"0.91\");\n  });\n\n  it(\"marks validate as ran only when a value exists, regardless of source\", () => {\n    const noValue = deriveRuleTrace(row({ appliedRuleId: \"rule-1\", proposedValue: \"\" }));\n    expect(noValue.find((s) => s.node === \"validate\")!.ran).toBe(false);\n  });\n\n  it(\"falls back to appliedRuleId when appliedRuleStrategy is null\", () => {\n    const trace = deriveRuleTrace(row({ appliedRuleId: \"rule-9\", appliedRuleStrategy: null, proposedValue: \"X\" }));\n    expect(trace[0].detail).toContain(\"rule-9\");\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n",
        "level": 2
      },
      {
        "title": "5. `lib/audit-detail.ts` — `auditDetailParts`, `auditDetailLine`, `auditNote`",
        "content": "\nAn 11-branch flattener over an untyped `jsonb` blob. **This is the highest-value gap in the pure-logic layer** — it silently drops anything it doesn't recognize, and every branch has a \"which fields are present\" combinatorial question.\n\n**Gaps:** empty detail object → empty array; each individual key in isolation; `from === to` (dedup — shows one value, not `X → X`); `from` without `to` and vice versa; unknown/garbage keys ignored; non-string/non-number types in typed fields (e.g. `field: 123`) rejected by `str`/`num` guards; `count` with no matching `COUNT_NOUN` entry (falls back to bare number); `previousStatus` underscore-to-hyphen replacement; `auditNote` returns null when absent.\n\n```ts\n// lib/audit-detail.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { auditDetailParts, auditDetailLine, auditNote } from \"@/lib/audit-detail\";\nimport type { AuditEntry } from \"@/types/resolution\";\n\nfunction entry(detail: Record<string, unknown>, action: AuditEntry[\"action\"] = \"resolution_proposed\"): AuditEntry {\n  return { id: \"1\", runId: \"r1\", resolutionId: null, action, actor: \"j.rao\", detail, createdAt: new Date() } as AuditEntry;\n}\n\ndescribe(\"auditDetailParts\", () => {\n  it(\"returns an empty array for an empty detail object\", () => {\n    expect(auditDetailParts(entry({}))).toEqual([]);\n  });\n\n  it(\"ignores keys it does not recognize\", () => {\n    expect(auditDetailParts(entry({ someUnknownKey: \"x\" }))).toEqual([]);\n  });\n\n  it(\"ignores wrong-typed values in typed fields\", () => {\n    expect(auditDetailParts(entry({ confidence: \"high\" }))).toEqual([]); // string, not number\n  });\n\n  it(\"shows externalId then field\", () => {\n    expect(auditDetailParts(entry({ externalId: \"ACC-4417\", field: \"parentExternalId\" }))).toEqual([\"ACC-4417\", \"parentExternalId\"]);\n  });\n\n  it(\"shows 'from → to' only when they differ\", () => {\n    expect(auditDetailParts(entry({ proposedValue: \"A\", chosenValue: \"B\" }))).toContain(\"A → B\");\n  });\n\n  it(\"collapses to a single value when proposed equals chosen\", () => {\n    const parts = auditDetailParts(entry({ proposedValue: \"A\", chosenValue: \"A\" }));\n    expect(parts).toContain(\"A\");\n    expect(parts).not.toContain(\"A → A\");\n  });\n\n  it(\"shows chosenValue alone when there is no proposedValue (override with no proposal)\", () => {\n    expect(auditDetailParts(entry({ chosenValue: \"B\" }))).toEqual([\"B\"]);\n  });\n\n  it(\"uses COUNT_NOUN for known actions\", () => {\n    const parts = auditDetailParts(entry({ count: 12 }, \"conflict_detected\"));\n    expect(parts).toContain(\"12 conflicts\");\n  });\n\n  it(\"falls back to a bare formatted number for actions with no noun mapping\", () => {\n    const parts = auditDetailParts(entry({ count: 12 }, \"run_started\"));\n    expect(parts).toContain(\"12\");\n  });\n\n  it(\"replaces underscores in previousStatus\", () => {\n    expect(auditDetailParts(entry({ previousStatus: \"auto_applied\" }))).toContain(\"was auto-applied\");\n  });\n\n  it(\"indicates a note exists without inlining its text\", () => {\n    const parts = auditDetailParts(entry({ note: \"reviewed twice\" }));\n    expect(parts).toContain(\"note attached\");\n    expect(parts.join(\" \")).not.toContain(\"reviewed twice\");\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"auditDetailLine\", () => {\n  it(\"joins with a middot separator\", () => {\n    expect(auditDetailLine(entry({ externalId: \"ACC-1\", field: \"name\" }))).toBe(\"ACC-1 · name\");\n  });\n  it(\"returns null when nothing was recognized\", () => {\n    expect(auditDetailLine(entry({}))).toBeNull();\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"auditNote\", () => {\n  it(\"returns the raw note text\", () => expect(auditNote(entry({ note: \"hi\" }))).toBe(\"hi\"));\n  it(\"returns null when absent\", () => expect(auditNote(entry({}))).toBeNull());\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n",
        "level": 2
      },
      {
        "title": "6. `lib/uuid.ts` — `isUuid`",
        "content": "\nUsed as a **security/routing gate** on every dynamic API param (`isUuid(conflictId)`, `isUuid(sourceId)`, `isUuid(runId)`) to prevent a malformed param from reaching Postgres as a cast error. Zero tests on the regex itself.\n\n```ts\n// lib/uuid.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { isUuid } from \"@/lib/uuid\";\n\ndescribe(\"isUuid\", () => {\n  it(\"accepts a canonical lowercase v4 UUID\", () => {\n    expect(isUuid(\"a41f1234-c9ab-4d3e-8f21-abcdef123456\")).toBe(true);\n  });\n  it(\"accepts uppercase hex\", () => {\n    expect(isUuid(\"A41F1234-C9AB-4D3E-8F21-ABCDEF123456\")).toBe(true);\n  });\n  it(\"rejects a non-UUID path segment\", () => {\n    expect(isUuid(\"banana\")).toBe(false);\n  });\n  it(\"rejects missing hyphens\", () => {\n    expect(isUuid(\"a41f1234c9ab4d3e8f21abcdef123456\")).toBe(false);\n  });\n  it(\"rejects SQL-injection-shaped input without throwing\", () => {\n    expect(isUuid(\"'; DROP TABLE runs; --\")).toBe(false);\n  });\n  it(\"rejects empty string\", () => expect(isUuid(\"\")).toBe(false));\n  it(\"rejects a UUID with extra trailing characters\", () => {\n    expect(isUuid(\"a41f1234-c9ab-4d3e-8f21-abcdef123456x\")).toBe(false);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n",
        "level": 2
      },
      {
        "title": "7. `lib/reviewer-label.ts` — `reviewerLabel`",
        "content": "\n```ts\n// lib/reviewer-label.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { reviewerLabel } from \"@/lib/reviewer-label\";\n\ndescribe(\"reviewerLabel\", () => {\n  it(\"prefers username over email\", () => {\n    expect(reviewerLabel({ username: \"j.rao\", primaryEmailAddress: { emailAddress: \"j@x.com\" } }, \"fallback\")).toBe(\"j.rao\");\n  });\n  it(\"falls back to email when username is missing\", () => {\n    expect(reviewerLabel({ username: null, primaryEmailAddress: { emailAddress: \"j@x.com\" } }, \"fallback\")).toBe(\"j@x.com\");\n  });\n  it(\"falls back to the provided fallback when user is null\", () => {\n    expect(reviewerLabel(null, \"user_123\")).toBe(\"user_123\");\n  });\n  it(\"falls back when both username and email are absent\", () => {\n    expect(reviewerLabel({ username: null, primaryEmailAddress: null }, \"user_123\")).toBe(\"user_123\");\n  });\n  it(\"falls back when username is an empty string (falsy-but-defined edge case)\", () => {\n    // `??` does not treat \"\" as nullish — document actual behavior.\n    expect(reviewerLabel({ username: \"\", primaryEmailAddress: { emailAddress: \"j@x.com\" } }, \"fallback\")).toBe(\"\");\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n",
        "level": 2
      },
      {
        "title": "8. `lib/api-client.ts` — `postJson`/`patchJson`/`sendJson`",
        "content": "\nClient-side network layer with three distinct failure modes: network failure, non-JSON response, non-2xx with a structured error body. Needs `fetch` mocking.\n\n```ts\n// lib/api-client.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect, vi, afterEach } from \"vitest\";\nimport { postJson, patchJson } from \"@/lib/api-client\";\n\nafterEach(() => vi.restoreAllMocks());\n\ndescribe(\"postJson / patchJson\", () => {\n  it(\"returns ok:true with parsed data on 2xx\", async () => {\n    vi.stubGlobal(\"fetch\", vi.fn().mockResolvedValue({ ok: true, json: async () => ({ id: \"1\" }) }));\n    const r = await postJson<{ id: string }>(\"/api/x\", { a: 1 });\n    expect(r).toEqual({ ok: true, data: { id: \"1\" } });\n  });\n\n  it(\"surfaces a network failure without throwing\", async () => {\n    vi.stubGlobal(\"fetch\", vi.fn().mockRejectedValue(new TypeError(\"network\")));\n    const r = await postJson(\"/api/x\", {});\n    expect(r.ok).toBe(false);\n    if (!r.ok) expect(r.message).toMatch(/reach the server/i);\n  });\n\n  it(\"uses the server error message on a structured 400\", async () => {\n    vi.stubGlobal(\"fetch\", vi.fn().mockResolvedValue({\n      ok: false, status: 400, json: async () => ({ error: \"Bad field.\", issues: { field: \"required\" } }),\n    }));\n    const r = await patchJson(\"/api/x\", {});\n    expect(r).toEqual({ ok: false, message: \"Bad field.\", issues: { field: \"required\" } });\n  });\n\n  it(\"falls back to a generic status message when the error body is not JSON\", async () => {\n    vi.stubGlobal(\"fetch\", vi.fn().mockResolvedValue({ ok: false, status: 500, json: async () => { throw new Error(\"not json\"); } }));\n    const r = await postJson(\"/api/x\", {});\n    expect(r.ok).toBe(false);\n    if (!r.ok) expect(r.message).toBe(\"Request failed (500).\");\n  });\n\n  it(\"uses PATCH method for patchJson\", async () => {\n    const fetchMock = vi.fn().mockResolvedValue({ ok: true, json: async () => ({}) });\n    vi.stubGlobal(\"fetch\", fetchMock);\n    await patchJson(\"/api/x\", {});\n    expect(fetchMock.mock.calls[0][1].method).toBe(\"PATCH\");\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n",
        "level": 2
      },
      {
        "title": "9. `lib/server/crypto.ts` — the highest-risk untested file in the repo",
        "content": "\nEnvelope encryption for stored credentials. **This should be the #1 priority.** No unit test verifies the AES-GCM round trip, the AAD binding, or any of the three custom error paths.\n\n**Gaps:**\n- `encryptSecrets` → `decryptSecrets` round trip preserves the payload\n- Decrypting with the **wrong `sourceId`** (AAD mismatch) throws `CredentialDecryptError`, not silently succeeds — this is the core security property of the module\n- Tampered ciphertext byte fails GCM auth tag check\n- Malformed `iv`/`authTag` length rejected before attempting decrypt\n- `deriveKey`: valid 32-byte base64 key used directly; non-32-byte key hashed in dev, throws in `NODE_ENV=production`\n- `keyFor` throws `CredentialKeyError` with the right env var name when unset, and caches on second call\n- `sealToken`/`openToken` round trip; wrong `purpose` fails to open; malformed token (wrong part count, non-numeric version) returns `null` instead of throwing\n- `safeEqual`: equal strings, different-length strings (non-constant-time path), equal-length-but-different strings\n- `pkceChallenge` produces the correct S256 value for a known vector (RFC 7636 test vector)\n\n```ts\n// lib/server/crypto.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect, beforeEach, vi } from \"vitest\";\n\nconst GOOD_KEY = Buffer.alloc(32, 7).toString(\"base64\");\n\nasync function freshModule(env: Record<string, string | undefined>) {\n  vi.resetModules();\n  for (const [k, v] of Object.entries(env)) {\n    if (v === undefined) delete process.env[k];\n    else process.env[k] = v;\n  }\n  return import(\"@/lib/server/crypto\");\n}\n\ndescribe(\"encryptSecrets / decryptSecrets\", () => {\n  beforeEach(() => { process.env.CANON_CREDENTIAL_KEY = GOOD_KEY; });\n\n  it(\"round-trips a secret payload\", async () => {\n    const { encryptSecrets, decryptSecrets } = await freshModule({ CANON_CREDENTIAL_KEY: GOOD_KEY });\n    const sealed = encryptSecrets({ password: \"hunter2\" }, { sourceId: \"src-1\" });\n    expect(decryptSecrets(sealed, { sourceId: \"src-1\" })).toEqual({ password: \"hunter2\" });\n  });\n\n  it(\"fails to decrypt under a different sourceId (AAD binding)\", async () => {\n    const { encryptSecrets, decryptSecrets, CredentialDecryptError } = await freshModule({ CANON_CREDENTIAL_KEY: GOOD_KEY });\n    const sealed = encryptSecrets({ password: \"hunter2\" }, { sourceId: \"src-1\" });\n    expect(() => decryptSecrets(sealed, { sourceId: \"src-2\" })).toThrow(CredentialDecryptError);\n  });\n\n  it(\"fails to decrypt tampered ciphertext\", async () => {\n    const { encryptSecrets, decryptSecrets, CredentialDecryptError } = await freshModule({ CANON_CREDENTIAL_KEY: GOOD_KEY });\n    const sealed = encryptSecrets({ password: \"hunter2\" }, { sourceId: \"src-1\" });\n    const tampered = { ...sealed, ciphertext: sealed.ciphertext.slice(0, -4) + \"abcd\" };\n    expect(() => decryptSecrets(tampered, { sourceId: \"src-1\" })).toThrow(CredentialDecryptError);\n  });\n\n  it(\"rejects a malformed iv/authTag length before touching the cipher\", async () => {\n    const { encryptSecrets, decryptSecrets } = await freshModule({ CANON_CREDENTIAL_KEY: GOOD_KEY });\n    const sealed = encryptSecrets({ x: \"y\" }, { sourceId: \"s\" });\n    expect(() => decryptSecrets({ ...sealed, iv: \"AA\" }, { sourceId: \"s\" })).toThrow();\n  });\n\n  it(\"uses a 32-byte base64 key directly\", async () => {\n    const { credentialEncryptionReady } = await freshModule({ CANON_CREDENTIAL_KEY: GOOD_KEY });\n    expect(credentialEncryptionReady()).toBe(true);\n  });\n\n  it(\"throws CredentialKeyError when the key env var is unset\", async () => {\n    const { credentialEncryptionReady } = await freshModule({ CANON_CREDENTIAL_KEY: undefined });\n    expect(credentialEncryptionReady()).toBe(false);\n  });\n\n  it(\"refuses a short key in production instead of hashing it\", async () => {\n    const { encryptSecrets, CredentialKeyError } = await freshModule({ CANON_CREDENTIAL_KEY: \"short\", NODE_ENV: \"production\" });\n    expect(() => encryptSecrets({ a: \"b\" }, { sourceId: \"s\" })).toThrow(CredentialKeyError);\n  });\n\n  it(\"hashes a non-32-byte key to length outside production, with a warning\", async () => {\n    const warn = vi.spyOn(console, \"warn\").mockImplementation(() => {});\n    const { encryptSecrets, decryptSecrets } = await freshModule({ CANON_CREDENTIAL_KEY: \"short-passphrase\", NODE_ENV: \"development\" });\n    const sealed = encryptSecrets({ a: \"b\" }, { sourceId: \"s\" });\n    expect(decryptSecrets(sealed, { sourceId: \"s\" })).toEqual({ a: \"b\" });\n    expect(warn).toHaveBeenCalled();\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"sealToken / openToken\", () => {\n  it(\"round-trips a payload for the same purpose\", async () => {\n    const { sealToken, openToken } = await freshModule({ CANON_CREDENTIAL_KEY: GOOD_KEY });\n    const token = sealToken({ nonce: \"abc\", sourceId: \"s1\" }, \"oauth-state\");\n    expect(openToken(token, \"oauth-state\")).toEqual({ nonce: \"abc\", sourceId: \"s1\" });\n  });\n\n  it(\"returns null when opened with the wrong purpose\", async () => {\n    const { sealToken, openToken } = await freshModule({ CANON_CREDENTIAL_KEY: GOOD_KEY });\n    const token = sealToken({ nonce: \"abc\" }, \"oauth-state\");\n    expect(openToken(token, \"other-purpose\")).toBeNull();\n  });\n\n  it(\"returns null for a malformed token (wrong segment count)\", async () => {\n    const { openToken } = await freshModule({ CANON_CREDENTIAL_KEY: GOOD_KEY });\n    expect(openToken(\"v1.only.two\", \"oauth-state\")).toBeNull();\n  });\n\n  it(\"returns null for a non-numeric version prefix\", async () => {\n    const { openToken } = await freshModule({ CANON_CREDENTIAL_KEY: GOOD_KEY });\n    expect(openToken(\"vX.a.b.c\", \"oauth-state\")).toBeNull();\n  });\n\n  it(\"never throws on garbage input\", async () => {\n    const { openToken } = await freshModule({ CANON_CREDENTIAL_KEY: GOOD_KEY });\n    expect(() => openToken(\"not-a-token-at-all\", \"oauth-state\")).not.toThrow();\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"safeEqual\", () => {\n  it(\"returns true for equal strings\", async () => {\n    const { safeEqual } = await freshModule({ CANON_CREDENTIAL_KEY: GOOD_KEY });\n    expect(safeEqual(\"abc\", \"abc\")).toBe(true);\n  });\n  it(\"returns false for different-length strings without throwing\", async () => {\n    const { safeEqual } = await freshModule({ CANON_CREDENTIAL_KEY: GOOD_KEY });\n    expect(safeEqual(\"abc\", \"abcd\")).toBe(false);\n  });\n  it(\"returns false for same-length but different strings\", async () => {\n    const { safeEqual } = await freshModule({ CANON_CREDENTIAL_KEY: GOOD_KEY });\n    expect(safeEqual(\"abc\", \"abd\")).toBe(false);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"pkceChallenge\", () => {\n  it(\"matches the RFC 7636 appendix B test vector\", async () => {\n    const { pkceChallenge } = await freshModule({ CANON_CREDENTIAL_KEY: GOOD_KEY });\n    expect(pkceChallenge(\"dBjftJeZ4CVP-mB92K27uhbUJU1p1r_wW1gFWFOEjXk\"))\n      .toBe(\"E9Melhoa2OwvFrEMTJguCHaoeK1t8URWbuGJSstw-cM\");\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n",
        "level": 2
      },
      {
        "title": "10. `lib/server/credentials.ts`, `oauth.ts`, `rulesets.ts` — need DB mocking",
        "content": "\nThese are entangled with Drizzle (`getDb()`), so they're **integration** rather than pure-unit targets. Currently 0% covered including the non-DB logic embedded in them.\n\n**Gaps (mockable without a real DB, via `vi.mock(\"@/lib/db\")`):**\n- `secretKeyNames`: OAuth method returns `[\"accessToken\", \"refreshToken\"]` regardless of schema; other methods derive from `spec.fields` filtered by `sensitivity === \"secret\"`; unknown `(kind, method)` pair returns `[]`\n- `isExpired`: null `expiresAt` → never expired; past date → expired; exact boundary (`expiresAt === now`) → expired (uses `<=`)\n- `credentialsMissingFor`: sources needing no credentials (`synthetic`) excluded up front; empty input array short-circuits without a query\n\n- `resolveOAuth`: missing `clientIdEnv` throws `OAuthConfigError` naming the exact env var; missing required `clientSecretEnv` throws; a method with no `oauth` spec throws\n- `redirectUri`: `CANON_APP_URL` set → uses it (trailing slash stripped); unset → falls back to request origin\n- `render`: multiple `{key}` substitutions in one template; a key not present in `values` left as literal `{key}` (undocumented behavior worth locking down)\n- `verifyState`: valid cookie+state → returns pending; missing cookie → null; state mismatch → null (constant-time); `kind` mismatch between path and sealed state → null; malformed `publicValues` JSON inside the sealed token → null\n- `readGrant`: missing `access_token` throws; `expires_in` converted to an absolute `Date`; absent `expires_in` → `expiresAt: null`\n- `describeOAuthError`: extracts `error_description`/`message`/`error` in priority order; non-object payload → null\n\n- `createRulesetVersion`: version numbers increment per-name (not globally); first ruleset for a new name gets version 1; creating a new version deactivates the previously active one; concurrent-save serialization via advisory lock (integration-level, hard to unit test — flag as an integration gap requiring a real Postgres transaction test)\n\n```ts\n// lib/server/oauth.test.ts (representative — apply same pattern to credentials.ts / rulesets.ts)\nimport { describe, it, expect, vi, beforeEach } from \"vitest\";\nimport { resolveOAuth, redirectUri, verifyState, OAuthConfigError } from \"@/lib/server/oauth\";\n\ndescribe(\"resolveOAuth\", () => {\n  beforeEach(() => { delete process.env.SALESFORCE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID; });\n\n  it(\"throws OAuthConfigError naming the missing client id env var\", () => {\n    expect(() => resolveOAuth(\"salesforce\", \"oauth2\")).toThrow(/SALESFORCE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID/);\n  });\n\n  it(\"throws when a required client secret is missing\", () => {\n    process.env.SALESFORCE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID = \"id\";\n    expect(() => resolveOAuth(\"salesforce\", \"oauth2\")).toThrow(OAuthConfigError);\n  });\n\n  it(\"succeeds for a public-client provider with no secret env configured (Databricks)\", () => {\n    process.env.DATABRICKS_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID = \"id\";\n    expect(() => resolveOAuth(\"databricks\", \"oauth2\")).not.toThrow();\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"redirectUri\", () => {\n  it(\"prefers CANON_APP_URL and strips trailing slashes\", () => {\n    process.env.CANON_APP_URL = \"https://canon.example.com/\";\n    expect(redirectUri(\"salesforce\", \"https://ignored/x\")).toBe(\"https://canon.example.com/api/oauth/salesforce/callback\");\n  });\n  it(\"falls back to the request origin when unset\", () => {\n    delete process.env.CANON_APP_URL;\n    expect(redirectUri(\"salesforce\", \"http://localhost:3000/api/oauth/salesforce/authorize\")).toBe(\n      \"http://localhost:3000/api/oauth/salesforce/callback\",\n    );\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"verifyState\", () => {\n  it(\"returns null when the cookie is missing\", () => {\n    expect(verifyState(undefined, \"state123\", \"salesforce\")).toBeNull();\n  });\n  it(\"returns null on a nonce mismatch\", () => {\n    // TODO: seal a real token with sealToken(), then pass a different returnedState\n  });\n  it(\"returns null when the sealed kind does not match the path kind\", () => {\n    // TODO: seal a token for \"hubspot\", call verifyState(cookie, state, \"salesforce\")\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n",
        "level": 2
      },
      {
        "title": "11. `lib/server/conflicts.ts` — `recordReview` (the core write path)",
        "content": "\nThis is the single most important business-logic function in the app and has **zero tests**. It needs `vi.mock(\"@/lib/db\")` and `vi.mock(\"@/lib/server/audit\")`.\n\n**Gaps:**\n- Conflict not found → `404`\n- Conflict found but `resolution` is `null` (run still resolving) → `409`\n- `approve` action when `proposedValue` is empty (escalated, nothing to approve) → `409`, distinct message\n- `override` action with a value that fails `checkObservedValue` → `400`, message passed through unchanged\n- `override` action stores the **folded/matched** observed value, not the raw typed input\n- `reject` action: `chosenValue` in the audit detail is explicitly `null` regardless of `proposedValue`\n- Successful `approve`: `overrideValue` cleared to `null`, `status` set from `REVIEW_RESULT_STATUS`, `reviewedBy` from `reviewer.label` (never from a caller-supplied field)\n- Audit entry `previousStatus` reflects the resolution's status **before** the update\n- Audit `note`: empty string treated as absent (`null`), non-empty passed through\n\n```ts\n// lib/server/conflicts.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect, vi, beforeEach } from \"vitest\";\n\nconst mockDb = { update: vi.fn(), select: vi.fn() /* ... */ };\nvi.mock(\"@/lib/db\", () => ({ getDb: () => mockDb }));\nconst appendAudit = vi.fn();\nvi.mock(\"@/lib/server/audit\", () => ({ appendAudit }));\n\n// getReviewTarget itself hits the DB via baseQuery(); for a unit test, mock\n// `getReviewTarget` directly rather than the whole Drizzle chain.\nimport * as conflictsModule from \"@/lib/server/conflicts\";\n\ndescribe(\"recordReview\", () => {\n  beforeEach(() => vi.clearAllMocks());\n\n  it(\"returns 404 when the conflict does not exist\", async () => {\n    vi.spyOn(conflictsModule, \"getReviewTarget\").mockResolvedValue(null);\n    const result = await conflictsModule.recordReview({ conflictId: \"missing\", action: { action: \"approve\" }, reviewer: { userId: \"u1\", label: \"j.rao\" } });\n    expect(result).toEqual({ ok: false, code: 404, message: \"No such conflict.\" });\n  });\n\n  it(\"returns 409 when nothing has been proposed yet (resolution is null)\", async () => {\n    vi.spyOn(conflictsModule, \"getReviewTarget\").mockResolvedValue({\n      conflictId: \"c1\", runId: \"r1\", field: \"name\", externalId: \"ACC-1\", severity: 2, observed: [\"A\", \"B\"], resolution: null,\n    });\n    const result = await conflictsModule.recordReview({ conflictId: \"c1\", action: { action: \"approve\" }, reviewer: { userId: \"u1\", label: \"j.rao\" } });\n    expect(result.ok).toBe(false);\n    if (!result.ok) expect(result.code).toBe(409);\n  });\n\n  it(\"rejects approving an escalated conflict with no proposed value\", async () => {\n    vi.spyOn(conflictsModule, \"getReviewTarget\").mockResolvedValue({\n      conflictId: \"c1\", runId: \"r1\", field: \"name\", externalId: \"ACC-1\", severity: 2, observed: [\"A\", \"B\"],\n      resolution: { id: \"res1\", proposedValue: \"\", appliedRuleId: null, confidence: 0, status: \"escalated\" },\n    });\n    const result = await conflictsModule.recordReview({ conflictId: \"c1\", action: { action: \"approve\" }, reviewer: { userId: \"u1\", label: \"j.rao\" } });\n    expect(result.ok).toBe(false);\n    if (!result.ok) expect(result.message).toMatch(/no value was proposed/i);\n  });\n\n  it(\"rejects an override value that is neither observed value nor a legal normalization\", async () => {\n    vi.spyOn(conflictsModule, \"getReviewTarget\").mockResolvedValue({\n      conflictId: \"c1\", runId: \"r1\", field: \"name\", externalId: \"ACC-1\", severity: 2, observed: [\"Acme Inc.\", \"ACME\"],\n      resolution: { id: \"res1\", proposedValue: \"Acme Inc.\", appliedRuleId: null, confidence: 0, status: \"escalated\" },\n    });\n    const result = await conflictsModule.recordReview({\n      conflictId: \"c1\", action: { action: \"override\", overrideValue: \"Totally Different Co\" }, reviewer: { userId: \"u1\", label: \"j.rao\" },\n    });\n    expect(result.ok).toBe(false);\n    if (!result.ok) expect(result.code).toBe(400);\n  });\n\n  it(\"stores the folded/matched value on a valid override, not the raw typed input\", async () => {\n    // Assert `overrideValue` written to the DB equals check.matches, not action.overrideValue.\n  });\n\n  it(\"sets chosenValue to null in the audit detail on reject, even if a value was proposed\", async () => {\n    // Assert appendAudit call's detail.chosenValue === null when action.action === \"reject\".\n  });\n\n  it(\"clears reviewedBy from the session, never from the request body\", async () => {\n    // Assert the reviewer passed in — not anything on `action` — becomes reviewedBy.\n  });\n});\n```\n\nAlso untested in the same file: `toQueueRow` (orphan-side presence logic, `sourceName` fallback to `\"unknown source\"` for an entity belonging to neither run source, `splitValues` newline handling with blank lines/whitespace-only lines), `getQueueCounts` (facet-excludes-itself counting), `filters`/`omit` behavior.\n\n---\n\n",
        "level": 2
      },
      {
        "title": "12. `lib/server/export.ts` — `applyDecisions`, `appliedValue`, `decisionsToCsv`, `estimateExportBytes`",
        "content": "\nPure functions embedded in a DB-heavy file — extractable and directly testable without mocking.\n\n```ts\n// lib/server/export.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\n\ndescribe(\"appliedValue (via buildRunExport's exported helpers, or extract to lib/)\", () => {\n  it(\"returns null for a status not in APPLIED_STATUSES (escalated, proposed, rejected)\", () => {\n    // TODO: export `appliedValue` or test indirectly through loadDecisions\n  });\n  it(\"returns overrideValue when status is 'overridden'\", () => {});\n  it(\"returns proposedValue when status is 'auto_applied' or 'approved'\", () => {});\n});\n\ndescribe(\"applyDecisions\", () => {\n  it(\"leaves parentExternalId unchanged when no decision touches it\", () => {});\n  it(\"reparents when a parentExternalId decision has an appliedValue\", () => {});\n  it(\"marks reparented=false when the resolved value equals the original (no-op override)\", () => {});\n  it(\"ignores decisions on fields other than parentExternalId\", () => {});\n});\n\ndescribe(\"decisionsToCsv\", () => {\n  it(\"quotes fields containing commas, quotes, or newlines\", () => {});\n  it(\"escapes embedded double quotes by doubling them\", () => {});\n  it(\"renders null values as empty cells\", () => {});\n  it(\"ends every line with CRLF including the trailing line\", () => {});\n});\n\ndescribe(\"estimateExportBytes\", () => {\n  it(\"sums only the requested sections' byte estimates\", () => {});\n  it(\"returns 0 for an empty sections list\", () => {});\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n",
        "level": 2
      },
      {
        "title": "13. `types/queue.ts` — `conflictFieldLabel`, `severityReason`",
        "content": "\n```ts\n// types/queue.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { conflictFieldLabel, severityReason } from \"@/types/queue\";\n\ndescribe(\"conflictFieldLabel\", () => {\n  it(\"returns 'entity absent' for orphan class regardless of field\", () => {\n    expect(conflictFieldLabel({ field: \"name\", conflictClass: \"orphan\", a: { values: [], present: false }, b: { values: [\"x\"], present: true } })).toBe(\"entity absent\");\n  });\n\n  it(\"shows N → M for a duplicate that collapses record count\", () => {\n    expect(conflictFieldLabel({ field: \"x\", conflictClass: \"duplicate\", a: { values: [\"1\", \"2\"], present: true }, b: { values: [\"1\"], present: true } })).toBe(\"2 → 1\");\n  });\n\n  it(\"falls back to 'duplicate record' when counts are equal or one side is empty\", () => {\n    expect(conflictFieldLabel({ field: \"x\", conflictClass: \"duplicate\", a: { values: [\"1\"], present: true }, b: { values: [], present: false } })).toBe(\"duplicate record\");\n  });\n\n  it(\"returns the raw field name for a plain field conflict\", () => {\n    expect(conflictFieldLabel({ field: \"parentExternalId\", conflictClass: \"field\", a: { values: [\"A\"], present: true }, b: { values: [\"B\"], present: true } })).toBe(\"parentExternalId\");\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"severityReason\", () => {\n  it(\"explains structural conflicts\", () => {\n    expect(severityReason({ conflictClass: \"structural\", severity: 4, childCount: 0 })).toMatch(/rollups/);\n  });\n  it(\"distinguishes orphan-with-children from orphan-without\", () => {\n    expect(severityReason({ conflictClass: \"orphan\", severity: 4, childCount: 3 })).toContain(\"3 children\");\n    expect(severityReason({ conflictClass: \"orphan\", severity: 3, childCount: 1 })).toContain(\"1 child\"); // singular\n    expect(severityReason({ conflictClass: \"orphan\", severity: 3, childCount: 0 })).toContain(\"no children\");\n  });\n  it(\"distinguishes severity 3 from other non-structural severities on the default branch\", () => {\n    expect(severityReason({ conflictClass: \"field\", severity: 3, childCount: 0 })).toMatch(/owns or is credited/);\n    expect(severityReason({ conflictClass: \"field\", severity: 2, childCount: 0 })).toMatch(/non-rollup/);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n",
        "level": 2
      },
      {
        "title": "14. `types/credentials.ts` — `credentialValuesSchema` (derived Zod schema)",
        "content": "\nThe schema is *generated* from `fields`, which is exactly the kind of code that silently breaks when a field is added without updating the generator's assumptions.\n\n```ts\n// types/credentials.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { credentialValuesSchema, findAuthMethod, storeCredentialsSchema } from \"@/types/credentials\";\n\ndescribe(\"credentialValuesSchema\", () => {\n  it(\"requires all non-optional fields\", () => {\n    const spec = findAuthMethod(\"salesforce\", \"password\")!;\n    const r = credentialValuesSchema(spec).safeParse({ loginHost: \"x\", username: \"y\" }); // missing password\n    expect(r.success).toBe(false);\n  });\n\n  it(\"allows an optional field to be omitted\", () => {\n    const spec = findAuthMethod(\"salesforce\", \"password\")!;\n    const r = credentialValuesSchema(spec).safeParse({ loginHost: \"x\", username: \"y\", password: \"z\" }); // no securityToken\n    expect(r.success).toBe(true);\n  });\n\n  it(\"rejects unknown keys (strict object)\", () => {\n    const spec = findAuthMethod(\"hubspot\", \"token\")!;\n    const r = credentialValuesSchema(spec).safeParse({ accessToken: \"pat-1\", extraField: \"x\" });\n    expect(r.success).toBe(false);\n  });\n\n  it(\"rejects a value exceeding the field's maxLength\", () => {\n    const spec = findAuthMethod(\"snowflake\", \"keypair\")!;\n    const r = credentialValuesSchema(spec).safeParse({\n      account: \"a\", user: \"u\", warehouse: \"w\", privateKey: \"x\".repeat(9000),\n    });\n    expect(r.success).toBe(false);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"storeCredentialsSchema\", () => {\n  it(\"rejects method:oauth2 outright — it must go through the authorize flow\", () => {\n    const r = storeCredentialsSchema.safeParse({ kind: \"salesforce\", method: \"oauth2\", values: {} });\n    expect(r.success).toBe(false);\n  });\n\n  it(\"rejects an unsupported (kind, method) pair\", () => {\n    const r = storeCredentialsSchema.safeParse({ kind: \"hubspot\", method: \"keypair\", values: {} });\n    expect(r.success).toBe(false);\n  });\n\n  it(\"addresses value-level errors under values.<field>\", () => {\n    const r = storeCredentialsSchema.safeParse({ kind: \"hubspot\", method: \"token\", values: {} });\n    expect(r.success).toBe(false);\n    if (!r.success) expect(r.error.issues[0].path).toEqual([\"values\", \"accessToken\"]);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n",
        "level": 2
      },
      {
        "title": "15. `components/conflicts/use-review.ts` — the review hook",
        "content": "\nNeeds `@testing-library/react` + `renderHook`, plus mocks for `next/navigation`'s `useRouter` and `lib/api-client`.\n\n```ts\n// components/conflicts/use-review.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect, vi } from \"vitest\";\nimport { renderHook, act } from \"@testing-library/react\";\n\nconst refresh = vi.fn();\nvi.mock(\"next/navigation\", () => ({ useRouter: () => ({ refresh }) }));\nconst patchJson = vi.fn();\nvi.mock(\"@/lib/api-client\", () => ({ patchJson: (...args: unknown[]) => patchJson(...args) }));\n\nimport { useReview } from \"@/components/conflicts/use-review\";\n\ndescribe(\"useReview\", () => {\n  it(\"sets pendingId during the request and clears it after\", async () => {\n    patchJson.mockResolvedValue({ ok: true, data: { conflictId: \"c1\", status: \"approved\", reviewedBy: \"j.rao\" } });\n    const { result } = renderHook(() => useReview());\n    await act(async () => { await result.current.submit(\"c1\", { action: \"approve\" }); });\n    expect(result.current.pendingId).toBeNull();\n  });\n\n  it(\"stores the server-confirmed status in `decided`, not an optimistic guess\", async () => {\n    patchJson.mockResolvedValue({ ok: true, data: { conflictId: \"c1\", status: \"overridden\", reviewedBy: \"j.rao\" } });\n    const { result } = renderHook(() => useReview());\n    await act(async () => { await result.current.submit(\"c1\", { action: \"override\", overrideValue: \"X\" }); });\n    expect(result.current.decided[\"c1\"]).toEqual({ status: \"overridden\", reviewedBy: \"j.rao\" });\n  });\n\n  it(\"does not touch `decided` on a failed request (no rollback needed, nothing was set)\", async () => {\n    patchJson.mockResolvedValue({ ok: false, message: \"No such conflict.\" });\n    const { result } = renderHook(() => useReview());\n    await act(async () => { await result.current.submit(\"c1\", { action: \"approve\" }); });\n    expect(result.current.decided[\"c1\"]).toBeUndefined();\n  });\n\n  it(\"triggers router.refresh() only on success\", async () => {\n    patchJson.mockResolvedValue({ ok: false, message: \"err\" });\n    const { result } = renderHook(() => useReview());\n    await act(async () => { await result.current.submit(\"c1\", { action: \"approve\" }); });\n    expect(refresh).not.toHaveBeenCalled();\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n",
        "level": 2
      },
      {
        "title": "16. API route integration gaps",
        "content": "\nNone of the route handlers under `app/api/**` have integration tests. These are the actual contract surface and should be tested with a real (or Testcontainers) DB, or at minimum with `getDb` mocked at the module boundary. Priorities, in order:\n\n| Route | Missing coverage |\n|---|---|\n| `PATCH /api/conflicts/[conflictId]/resolution` | invalid UUID → 404; unauthenticated → 401 (via `requireReviewerForApi`); malformed body → 400 with `issues`; happy path for each of approve/reject/override |\n| `POST /api/runs` | `sourceAId === sourceBId` → 400; nonexistent source/ruleset ids → 400 with specific message; missing credentials → 400 naming the source(s), singular vs plural grammar (`has` vs `have`, `it` vs `them`); **engine unreachable path** — run still gets 201 but is recorded failed (`failUndispatchedRun` + audit `run_failed`) — currently completely unverified |\n| `GET /api/oauth/[kind]/authorize` | unknown `kind` → redirect to `/sources`; missing/invalid `sourceId` → redirect with error; source kind mismatch → redirect to connect screen; required field missing → redirect naming the field; **host field with a scheme/path (open-redirect guard)** — `isPlainHost` rejection is untested at the route level; cookie attributes (`httpOnly`, `sameSite=lax`, `secure` gated on `NODE_ENV`) |\n| `GET /api/oauth/[kind]/callback` | provider `error=access_denied` → friendly decline message; state cookie missing/mismatched → generic \"could not be verified\"; missing `code` param; `CredentialKeyError`/`OAuthConfigError`/`OAuthExchangeError` each redirect with their own `.message`; **state cookie is deleted exactly once, regardless of outcome** (currently unverified — a bug here would make the flow replayable) |\n| `PUT /api/sources/[sourceId]/credentials` | source `kind` mismatch with body `kind` → 400; unsupported auth method for the kind → 404; field split respects `sensitivity` from the schema, not the request; `CredentialKeyError` → 503 distinctly from a generic 500 |\n| `GET /api/audit/export`, `GET /api/runs/[runId]/export` | CSV cell escaping at the HTTP boundary (values containing commas/quotes/CRLF actually round-trip through a real response body); `content-disposition` filename correctness; invalid `sections` query param → 400; unknown `format` → 400 |\n| `GET /api/runs/[runId]/status` | terminal run status skips the engine call entirely (currently unverified — an easy regression to introduce); `cache-control: no-store` header present |\n\nSkeleton pattern (illustrative — route tests need Next's `Request`/route-context shape, most easily driven with `next/server`'s test utilities or a thin wrapper):\n\n```ts\n// app/api/runs/route.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect, vi, beforeEach } from \"vitest\";\n\nvi.mock(\"@/lib/server/auth\", () => ({ requireReviewerForApi: vi.fn() }));\nvi.mock(\"@/lib/server/sources\", () => ({ getSource: vi.fn() }));\nvi.mock(\"@/lib/server/rulesets\", () => ({ getRuleset: vi.fn() }));\nvi.mock(\"@/lib/server/credentials\", () => ({ credentialsMissingFor: vi.fn() }));\nvi.mock(\"@/lib/server/runs\", () => ({ createRun: vi.fn(), listRuns: vi.fn(), failUndispatchedRun: vi.fn() }));\nvi.mock(\"@/lib/server/engine\", () => ({ startRun: vi.fn(), EngineUnreachableError: class extends Error {} }));\nvi.mock(\"@/lib/server/audit\", () => ({ appendAudit: vi.fn() }));\n\nimport { POST } from \"@/app/api/runs/route\";\nimport { requireReviewerForApi } from \"@/lib/server/auth\";\nimport { getSource } from \"@/lib/server/sources\";\nimport { getRuleset } from \"@/lib/server/rulesets\";\nimport { credentialsMissingFor } from \"@/lib/server/credentials\";\n\ndescribe(\"POST /api/runs\", () => {\n  beforeEach(() => {\n    vi.mocked(requireReviewerForApi).mockResolvedValue({ ok: true, reviewer: { userId: \"u1\", label: \"j.rao\" } });\n  });\n\n  it(\"rejects sourceAId === sourceBId before any DB lookup\", async () => {\n    const req = new Request(\"http://x/api/runs\", { method: \"POST\", body: JSON.stringify({ sourceAId: \"s1\", sourceBId: \"s1\", rulesetId: \"r1\" }) });\n    const res = await POST(req);\n    expect(res.status).toBe(400);\n    expect(getSource).not.toHaveBeenCalled();\n  });\n\n  it(\"records a failed run (not a 500) when the engine is unreachable\", async () => {\n    vi.mocked(getSource).mockResolvedValue({ id: \"s1\", kind: \"salesforce\", name: \"SF\" } as any);\n    vi.mocked(getRuleset).mockResolvedValue({ id: \"r1\" } as any);\n    vi.mocked(credentialsMissingFor).mockResolvedValue([]);\n    // TODO: mock createRun to return a run, startRun to throw EngineUnreachableError,\n    // then assert failUndispatchedRun + appendAudit(\"run_failed\") were called and\n    // the response is still 201 with the runId.\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n",
        "level": 2
      },
      {
        "title": "Summary — priority order",
        "content": "1. **Add Vitest** (blocking everything else).\n2. `lib/server/crypto.ts` — security-critical, zero coverage, AAD/tamper properties are the whole point of the module.\n3. `lib/validate-value.ts` — the hallucination guard on human overrides.\n4. `lib/server/conflicts.ts::recordReview` — the core write path, 5+ untested branches.\n5. `lib/audit-detail.ts` — 11-branch flattener, silent-drop-on-unknown-key behavior needs locking down.\n6. `lib/rule-trace.ts`, `lib/uuid.ts` — small, pure, currently trivial to cover.\n7. `lib/server/oauth.ts` — CSRF/state-verification logic (`verifyState`), open-redirect guard (`isPlainHost` in the authorize route).\n8. `lib/format.ts`, `lib/diff-chars.ts`, `types/queue.ts` — pure display logic, cheap insurance against regressions.\n9. API route integration tests, especially the engine-unreachable-on-run-create path and the OAuth callback's single-use cookie guarantee.\n10. `components/conflicts/use-review.ts` and other client hooks — lowest risk, do last.",
        "level": 2
      }
    ],
    "codeBlocks": [
      {
        "language": "json",
        "code": "// package.json\n\"devDependencies\": {\n  \"vitest\": \"^3\",\n  \"@vitejs/plugin-react\": \"^5\",\n  \"vite-tsconfig-paths\": \"^5\"\n},\n\"scripts\": {\n  \"test\": \"vitest run\",\n  \"test:watch\": \"vitest\"\n}"
      },
      {
        "language": "ts",
        "code": "// lib/diff-chars.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { diffSegments } from \"@/lib/diff-chars\";\n\ndescribe(\"diffSegments\", () => {\n  it(\"returns everything as prefix when values are identical\", () => {\n    expect(diffSegments(\"APAC\", \"APAC\")).toEqual({ prefix: \"APAC\", middle: \"\", suffix: \"\" });\n  });\n\n  it(\"finds a differing middle with shared head and tail\", () => {\n    expect(diffSegments(\"APAC\", \"APAC-SOUTH\")).toEqual({\n      prefix: \"APAC\", middle: \"\", suffix: \"\" // TODO: verify actual expected split (differs by length)\n    });\n  });\n\n  it(\"handles totally disjoint strings\", () => {\n    const r = diffSegments(\"ACC-4417\", \"ACC-2201\");\n    expect(r.prefix).toBe(\"ACC-2\");\n    // TODO: assert middle/suffix precisely\n  });\n\n  it(\"handles one side empty\", () => {\n    expect(diffSegments(\"\", \"ACME\")).toEqual({ prefix: \"\", middle: \"\", suffix: \"\" });\n  });\n\n  it(\"does not double-count overlapping prefix/suffix on repeated characters\", () => {\n    // \"aaa\" vs \"aa\" — prefix scan alone would claim prefix=2, suffix scan must\n    // respect `max - prefix` or it re-consumes the same characters.\n    const r = diffSegments(\"aaa\", \"aa\");\n    expect(r.prefix.length + r.middle.length + r.suffix.length).toBe(3);\n  });\n\n  it(\"handles unicode / combining characters without splitting a code point\", () => {\n    const r = diffSegments(\"café\", \"cafe\\u0301\"); // é vs e + combining accent\n    expect(r.prefix + r.middle + r.suffix).toBe(\"café\");\n  });\n\n  it(\"case sensitivity: differing case is a middle, not equality\", () => {\n    const r = diffSegments(\"ACME\", \"acme\");\n    expect(r.middle.length).toBeGreaterThan(0);\n  });\n});"
      },
      {
        "language": "ts",
        "code": "// lib/validate-value.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { foldValue, checkObservedValue, observedValues, LEGAL_SUFFIXES } from \"@/lib/validate-value\";\n\ndescribe(\"foldValue\", () => {\n  it(\"lowercases, strips punctuation, collapses whitespace\", () => {\n    expect(foldValue(\"ACME-INC\")).toBe(\"acme\");\n    expect(foldValue(\"Acme Inc.\")).toBe(\"acme\");\n  });\n\n  it(\"strips multiple legal suffixes in one pass\", () => {\n    expect(foldValue(\"Trellis Labs Pvt Ltd\")).toBe(\"trellis labs\");\n  });\n\n  it(\"does not strip a suffix that IS the whole value\", () => {\n    expect(foldValue(\"Ltd\")).toBe(\"ltd\");\n  });\n\n  it(\"prefers the longest matching suffix (pvt ltd over ltd)\", () => {\n    expect(foldValue(\"X Pvt Ltd\")).not.toContain(\"pvt\");\n  });\n\n  it(\"folds diacritics via NFKD\", () => {\n    expect(foldValue(\"Café\")).toBe(\"cafe\");\n  });\n\n  it(\"returns empty string for punctuation-only input\", () => {\n    expect(foldValue(\"...---\")).toBe(\"\");\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"checkObservedValue\", () => {\n  it(\"rejects an empty/whitespace-only candidate\", () => {\n    const r = checkObservedValue(\"   \", [\"ACC-4417\"]);\n    expect(r.ok).toBe(false);\n  });\n\n  it(\"rejects when observed has no real values (orphan side)\", () => {\n    const r = checkObservedValue(\"ACC-4417\", [\"\", \"  \"]);\n    expect(r.ok).toBe(false);\n  });\n\n  it(\"accepts an exact match even when a folded match also exists\", () => {\n    const r = checkObservedValue(\"ACME Inc.\", [\"ACME Inc.\", \"acme inc\"]);\n    expect(r).toEqual({ ok: true, matches: \"ACME Inc.\" });\n  });\n\n  it(\"accepts a legal normalization of an observed value\", () => {\n    const r = checkObservedValue(\"ACME\", [\"ACME Inc.\"]);\n    expect(r).toEqual({ ok: true, matches: \"ACME Inc.\" });\n  });\n\n  it(\"rejects a value that folds to neither observed value (hallucination guard)\", () => {\n    const r = checkObservedValue(\"ACC-9999\", [\"ACC-4417\", \"ACC-2201\"]);\n    expect(r.ok).toBe(false);\n    if (!r.ok) expect(r.reason).toContain(\"ACC-4417\");\n  });\n\n  it(\"trims the candidate before comparing\", () => {\n    const r = checkObservedValue(\"  ACC-4417  \", [\"ACC-4417\"]);\n    expect(r).toEqual({ ok: true, matches: \"ACC-4417\" });\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"observedValues\", () => {\n  it(\"flattens both sides and drops blank entries\", () => {\n    expect(observedValues({ a: { values: [\"X\", \"\"] }, b: { values: [\"Y\"] } })).toEqual([\"X\", \"Y\"]);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe.skip(\"cross-language parity with engine/pipeline/normalize.py::LEGAL_SUFFIXES\", () => {\n  // Integration gap: nothing asserts the TS list and the Python list stay\n  // identical. A fixture-based contract test (shared JSON list, or a snapshot\n  // compared against the Python module's output) would catch drift.\n  it(\"LEGAL_SUFFIXES matches the engine's list byte-for-byte\", () => {\n    expect(LEGAL_SUFFIXES).toEqual([/* load from engine/pipeline/normalize.py fixture */]);\n  });\n});"
      },
